      "title": "Four findings",
      "html": "<p>A: Evidence supports fair presentation with no material misstatement. B: A known departure is material but not pervasive. C: A known departure is material and pervasive. D: Evidence is unavailable and possible effects are material and pervasive.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "aud-m4-tbs1-ex2",
      "title": "Assumptions",
      "html": "<p>The auditor is independent. No law requires a different outcome. Consider ordinary financial-statement opinion consequences under the applicable auditing standard.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Opinion for A</h3><p>Sufficient evidence supports fair presentation.</p><h3>Opinion for B</h3><p>The known departure is material but not pervasive.</p><h3>Opinion for C</h3><p>The known departure is material and pervasive.</p><h3>Opinion for D</h3><p>The evidence limitation has potentially material and pervasive effects.</p>"
